From: Trames contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Require a Metal timestamp counter set for Vulkan queue timestamps

The upstream CPU completion-time fallback produces host results after encoding
has already copied zero to GPU buffers. Report no queue timestamp capability
when a timestamp counter set is unavailable. Real hardware-counter paths and
all original query algorithms are unchanged; occlusion queries remain usable.

--- a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.mm
+++ b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.mm
@@ -2203,7 +2203,7 @@
 		uint32_t qfIdx = 0;
 
 		qfProps.queueCount = kMVKQueueCountPerQueueFamily;
-		qfProps.timestampValidBits = 64;
+		qfProps.timestampValidBits = _timestampMTLCounterSet ? 64 : 0;
 		qfProps.minImageTransferGranularity = { 1, 1, 1};
 
 		// General-purpose queue family
@@ -3605,6 +3605,8 @@
 			}
 		}
 	}
+	// Completion-time CPU timestamps cannot feed GPU query copies.
+	_properties.limits.timestampComputeAndGraphics = (_timestampMTLCounterSet != nil);
 }
 
 // Determine whether Vulkan semaphores should use a MTLEvent, CPU callbacks, or should limit
